-- CK-04: the twin of the guard `tests/corpus/check/bad/TryDefaultCycle.beni`,
-- written while that guard's golden still pinned checker v1's place and text
-- (R5's structural review, S6): `y = x?` and then `y` and `x` in the
-- same position make `x`'s type contain itself, whichever shape `?` settles
-- on — ONE `infinite_type`, the `?` defaulted to `Result` and the cycle
-- reported, not silenced. Under checker v2 it is reported at the parameter
-- `x`, a binder (checker-v2.md §6.3, §8.2); checker v1 at 2bc9e22 reported
-- it at the body. Claimed under v2 by R5, promoted at the cut-over (R11),
-- when the guard was re-blessed to the same place.
f x =
    let
        y =
            x?
    in
    if True then
        y

    else
        x
